# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Kramak Lite — .gitignore
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# This is the DISTRIBUTION REPO — not a user project.
# Everything here is either source/distribution content
# or dogfooding artifacts that shouldn't ship.
#
# For user projects adopting Kramak, see the guidance
# in docs/GETTING-STARTED.md — the default recommendation
# is to TRACK almost everything in .kramak/ for full
# development continuity and process archaeology.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Kramak WAL Recovery ───────────────────────────────
# The ONLY file that should ALWAYS be ignored, everywhere.
# This is a Write-Ahead Log temp file used for atomic
# state updates during crash recovery. It is never valid
# after recovery completes.
.kramak/state.json.tmp

# ── Kramak Dogfooding Artifacts ───────────────────────
# These patterns exist because this is the DISTRIBUTION
# repo. If someone tests Kramak against this repo itself,
# the runtime artifacts should not be committed to the
# distribution. In a real USER project, these should
# generally be TRACKED (see GETTING-STARTED.md).
.kramak/state.json
.kramak/SESSION-LOG.md
.kramak/HUMAN-TASKS.md
.kramak/work-items/*.md
!.kramak/work-items/.gitkeep
.kramak/plans/*.md
!.kramak/plans/.gitkeep
.kramak/ledger/*.jsonl
!.kramak/ledger/.gitkeep
.kramak/inbox/*.md
!.kramak/inbox/INBOX.md
!.kramak/inbox/.gitkeep

# ── Temporary Directories ─────────────────────────────
temp/
tmp/

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ── IDE / Editor ──────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
